  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "superlative: the most + adjective",
      "title_form": "El superlativo: the most + adjetivo",
      "title_target": "The Superlative: the most + adjective",
      "description_md_form": "Usamos **the most + adjetivo** para decir que algo es **el/la más** en su grupo. Es la forma superlativa para adjetivos largos (de 2 o más sílabas) como *excellent* o *possible*.\n\n**Estructura:**\n\n`the most + adjetivo`\n\n**Ejemplos:**\n- *This is **the most excellent** option.* = Esta es la opción más excelente.\n- *She is **the most possible** candidate.* = Ella es la candidata más posible.\n\n**Importante:** Para adjetivos cortos (1 sílaba) como *top* o *worst*, usamos otra forma: *the top*, *the worst*. No decimos *the most top* ni *the most worst*.\n\n**Comparación:**\n- *good* → *the best* (irregular)\n- *bad* → *the worst* (irregular)\n- *excellent* → *the most excellent* (regular largo)",
      "description_md_target": "We use **the most + adjective** to say that something is **the most** in its group. It is the superlative form for long adjectives (2 or more syllables) like *excellent* or *possible*.\n\n**Structure:**\n\n`the most + adjective`\n\n**Examples:**\n- *This is **the most excellent** option.*\n- *She is **the most possible** candidate.*\n\n**Important:** For short adjectives (1 syllable) like *top* or *worst*, we use another form: *the top*, *the worst*. We do not say *the most top* or *the most worst*.\n\n**Comparison:**\n- *good* → *the best* (irregular)\n- *bad* → *the worst* (irregular)\n- *excellent* → *the most excellent* (regular long)",
      "grammar_structure": "the most + adjective",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "superlative_forms",
        "headers": [
          "Adjetivo",
          "Superlativo",
          "Uso"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "excellent",
            "the most excellent",
            "el más excelente"
          ],
          [
            "possible",
            "the most possible",
            "el más posible"
          ],
          [
            "top",
            "the top",
            "el mejor / el superior"
          ],
          [
            "worst",
            "the worst",
            "el peor"
          ]
        ]
      },
